{"title":"Career Roadmap · Fashion Technologist","role":"Fashion Technologist","summary":"A Fashion Technologist combines textile science, garment technology, manufacturing and digital tools to improve the design, development, testing, production and performance of apparel and textile products.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Fashion Technology / Textile Science"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Fashion Technology / Textile Science → Fashion Technologist"},{"type":"p","text":"A Fashion Technologist combines textile science, garment technology, manufacturing and digital tools to improve the design, development, testing, production and performance of apparel and textile products."},{"type":"p","text":"The role sits between fashion design, textile science, manufacturing, product development and technology. Modern fashion technologists increasingly work with 3D apparel software, digital sampling, smart textiles, sustainable materials, textile testing and data-driven product development."},{"type":"p","text":"This is a directly aligned career for B.Sc Fashion Technology / Textile Science."},{"type":"h","text":"Career facts"},{"type":"table","header":["Item","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Sc Fashion Technology / Textile Science"}],[{"text":"Entry career"},{"text":"Fashion Technologist"}],[{"text":"Career cluster"},{"text":"Fashion Technology · Textiles · Apparel Manufacturing"}],[{"text":"Strongest foundations"},{"text":"Textile science + garment technology + manufacturing"}],[{"text":"Important technical skills"},{"text":"Textile testing, garment construction, CAD, product development"}],[{"text":"Digital skills"},{"text":"CLO 3D, Browzwear, Adobe, CAD, Excel"}],[{"text":"Future skills"},{"text":"Smart textiles, sustainable materials, digital fashion"}],[{"text":"Long-term route"},{"text":"Fashion Technologist → Senior 